  "facts": [
    "Henry Hudson Bridge, designed by David B. Steinman, opened 1936 as world's longest plate girder arch, spanning Spuyten Duyvil Creek just east of Hudson River.",
    "In 2000, a decade‑long $160 million rehabilitation replaced original decks, reopened pedestrian path, removed toll booths, and added seismic upgrades, for the Henry Hudson Bridge, a landmark of New York infrastructure.",
    "Starting February 2024, Bronx residents with NYCSC E‑ZPass receive a full toll rebate, making the Henry Hudson Bridge the first MTA crossing to offer a 100 percent discount to local drivers."
